message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Chronos-AEGIS: A Cognitive Mission Intelligence (CMI) Framework for Explainable, Trust-Aware Reasoning over Cyber-Physical Systems"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gupta
    given-names: Adishree
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/1stsimplifycode/chronos-aegis"
abstract: >
  Chronos-AEGIS implements the Cognitive Mission Intelligence (CMI)
  framework formalized in the accompanying manuscript
  (paper/Chronos-AEGIS_CMI_Manuscript_v4.pdf): a Temporal Reasoning
  Memory Graph, Episodic Mission Memory, Structured AI Argumentation,
  Causal Mission Intelligence, Cognitive Cyber Reasoning, Mission-Aware
  Cyber Risk Propagation, Temporal Attack Graphs, an AI Patch Scheduler,
  a Mission Digital Twin, and Adaptive Learning / Continual Reasoning,
  together with an evaluation framework, benchmark suite, and
  reproducibility workflow. See paper/artifact/ for the artifact
  description and docs/traceability-matrix.md for a per-claim mapping
  from the manuscript to this implementation.
